;; A sheltered hollow under a stepped roof; a steady lift (columns 4-6)
;; rises from its floor to Q. West of it the homeward shaft (columns 1-3,
;; D50) falls from Q onto a small rock shelf jutting from the west wall at
;; row 9, a rose stone set in it like a trapdoor at (1,9) with two tiles of
;; lip and open sky beyond; under the shelf the gap drops on into E. The
;; way home, readable before H5 and open with it. Shut, the stone seals the
;; shaft: the gap under the shelf is one tile high and closed to the east
;; by the floor (4,10), so nothing climbs past it from E (the reverse route
;; SYSTEMS' replay found: wall kicks up E's west wall into the shaft, then
;; the lift). test-cloudstair-homeward floods it.
(room
  region: cloudstair
  at: (7 -1)
  title: "Sheltered Seeds"
  intent: "seed creatures rest in a sheltered hollow below the last grass: a breath"
  bed: (wind 0.3 water 0 air 0.5 drone 0.3)
  light: 1
  sun: 1
  grid:
  ("#   ^^^##################"
   "#   ^^^   ###############"
   "#   ^^^     #############"
   "#   ^^^       ###########"
   "#   ^^^         #########"
   "#   ^^^           #######"
   "#   ^^^             #####"
   "#   ^^^                  "
   "#   ^^^                  "
   "#o##^^^ |  ||  |  | |    "
   "#   #####################")
  things: ((seed at: (12 9) count: 3)
           ;; the shaft's rose stone (D50), a trapdoor in the shelf: shut,
           ;; the way home is sealed and nothing climbs up the shaft from E;
           ;; with H5 it opens as you come down onto it, and you drop
           ;; through the gap under the shelf to E
           (ring-stone at: (1 9) overtone: 5)
           (seed at: (5 5) count: 2))
  decor: auto)
